{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Start with the ETF sponsor’s website. Rule 6c-11 generally requires the fund to publish its **portfolio holdings**—the securities and other positions it holds—before the market opens each business day, typically in a downloadable file. Those holdings are not necessarily the **portfolio composition file (PCF)**: the PCF is the creation/redemption basket used in transactions with the fund, and it may differ from the portfolio, for example when the fund uses custom baskets.\n\nWithout NSCC participant access, ask the sponsor’s ETF capital-markets or operations team for the PCF for the date you need. Explain whether you want the standard or a particular custom basket and how you will use it; the sponsor may provide it, direct you to a data vendor, or decline or charge for access. Do not assume every fund makes its PCF freely available to the public."}}
